2.2. The vast majority of housing units in Monaco are in the private sector
In this section, housing units, regardless of their regulatory status, are distinguished by ownership: on one
side, the state -owned housing stock, consisting of homes owned by the Monegasque state, and on the
other, the private sector.
Tableau 11. Breakdown of housing units by district and sector in 2025
Source: Monaco Statistics – 2025 Population census
In 2025, the Principality has nearly 18,200 private dwellings (80.6%) and 4,380 state -owned dwellings
(19.4%). The Jardin Exotique is now the district with the largest number of state-owned dwellings (937).
Figure 18. Distribution of private and state-owned dwellings by district in 2025
Source: Monaco Statistics – 2025 Population census
There are significant disparities between districts in terms of state- owned dwellings. Fontvieille has the
highest share, with 37.9% of its housing stock belonging to the State, followed by Jardin Exotique, La
Condamine, and Les Moneghetti, where around three dwellings in ten are also state-owned.
Despite its 5,365 dwellings, Monte-Carlo has only 172 state-owned units, or 2.9%. Larvotto has the lowest
share of state-owned dwellings, at 1.1%.
